<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
	Indonesian UI string catalog; the English default is in values/strings.xml.  Format-level
	identifiers (ParamAngleX, …) stay verbatim.  A key absent here resolves to the English catalog,
	so this file may be filled in incrementally.

	Terminology.  The same terms as the English catalog, in these Indonesian renderings.  The user
	manual uses them too, so a string that disagrees with them is a bug.

	File: berkas.  Any file, or a file whose kind does not matter.

	Artwork, or Layered Artwork: artwork, or artwork berlapis where the layers are the point.  This
	covers a PSD, CLIP, or KRA.  Never berkas seni, seni sumber, or gambar sumber for one of these.

	Puppet: boneka.  The thing being edited and saved, whether it is a UMA, a CMO3, or a MOC3.  It
	replaces both dokumen and a bare model.  Say model boneka or berkas boneka only where boneka alone
	would be vague, such as the in-memory data against the file on disk.

	EXT: a sentence about one specific file type names its extension (UMA, PSD, CMO3, MOC3) instead
	of saying berkas.

	Area: area, followed by the space's title as its header shows it: area Sumber, area Parameter,
	area Viewport 2D.  Never panel or ruang for one of these.  A bare viewport stays the generic word.

	Drawable: drawable.  Never mesh seni or objek gambar.  Mesh: mesh, the geometry only; the object
	is drawable.  Vertex, edge, and face stay vertex, edge, and face.  Lattice: kisi, with titik for
	its points, never vertex.  Object: objek (a drawable, part, or deformer), and elemen for one
	vertex, edge, or face.  Deformer: deformer, as in deformer warp and deformer rotasi.

	Key: key.  Keyform: keyform.  Keyframe: keyframe, reserved for a future dopesheet and never used
	for a keyform parameter.  Never kunci or tombol for a key.

	Part: part.  Bagian stays the generic word for a portion and never names a part.  Guide Part:
	part panduan.  Never gambar panduan, and never sketsa for the name.

	Atlas: atlas tekstur or atlas, each one a halaman.  Texture: tekstur.  Tile: tile.  Gutter:
	padding, never margin, which is Margin.  Extrude: perluasan tepi, never ekstrusi, the 3D sense.

	Bind: ikat, as in terikat, tidak terikat, ikat ulang, and lepas ikatan.  Tautan and tautkan are
	only for pairing two parameters.  A glue that is re-bound is disambung ulang, a separate sense.

	Glue: lem, a noun, never the verb mengelem.  Blend Shape: blend shape, apart from the Blend Mode
	field, mode campuran.  Alpha Mode: mode alfa.  The mode names (Normal, Multiply, Screen, Over,
	Atop, Out) stay verbatim.  Opacity: opasitas.  Alpha Threshold: ambang alfa.  Multiply Color and
	Screen Color: warna Multiply and warna Screen.  Group Mode: mode grup, with Pass Through,
	Dikelompokkan, and Terisolasi.

	Pose: pose; Pose Mode is Mode Pose and the default pose is pose bawaan.  Cursor: Kursor 2D, never
	penunjuk or tetikus, which mean the mouse pointer.  Runtime: runtime.  Target: target.

	Export notice verbs: ditulis (written), dibawa (carried), disederhanakan (lowered),
	direkonsiliasi (reconcile), dibuat dari awal (synthesized), digabungkan (bundled), and tertutupi
	(shadowed).

	Style.  Address the user with a bare imperative ("Pilih properti"), and with Anda, capitalized,
	where a pronoun is needed; never kamu, kau, or lo.  Commands and titles follow EN's Title Case
	under the PUEBI title rule: dan, atau, di, ke, dari, untuk, dengan, yang, and pada stay lowercase
	unless first.  The modifier follows the noun (Viewport 2D, berkas UMA).  Never reduplicate for a
	plural; a number or semua, beberapa carries it.  Never put an Indonesian affix on an English
	loan (di-bind); use the Indonesian verb (diikat) or recast the sentence.  Use the KBBI forms of
	established loans (ekspor, impor, parameter, tekstur, opasitas, objek, rotasi) and keep other
	loans in English.  One space between sentences, “ ” for a quoted name, and … for an ellipsis.

	Left as they are: "source artwork" (the display mode that draws a drawable from its layer instead
	of the atlas) is artwork sumber, art is shorthand for what a drawable shows, and format-level
	names stay verbatim for interop (model3.json, ParamAngleX, and the like).
-->
